    headline: 'Acceptance proofs — RED→GREEN against a frozen oracle',
    summary: 'A green suite tells you it passes **now**; it does not tell you it ever failed — and a check that has never rejected anything has never demonstrated that it can. An **acceptance proof** is the narrow answer, **derived rather than stored**, and it says exactly one thing: one declared command **exited nonzero** and later **exited zero**, while the declared **oracle** bytes stayed identical and the declared **implementation** bytes moved. Process-level, never “a test failed” — a missing module, a bad config, an unresolvable interpreter or an inner signal death surfacing as `128+n` all exit nonzero, and every surface says so. **Declaration** rides on the goal (`maddu goal set --oracle "<glob>" --impl "<glob>"`, repeatable, shape-validated at the door); legacy goals without sets keep the exact pre-1.121 evaluation path, recording no receipts and adding no noise. **Observation** belongs to the two commands an operator invokes on purpose: `maddu orient` runs every verifiable condition of an acceptance-active goal exactly once per orient, serialized under the observation lock, with per-condition state derived from ONE post-observation verified read; `maddu loop ralph` adopts the goal’s conditions (`--from-goal`) or one ad-hoc acceptance, records an **iteration-0 baseline observation** so the RED exists before the first iterate can touch the work, and **refuses at the door** rather than iterating toward something it could never prove. **BREAKING:** bare `loop ralph --verify` without both `--oracle` and `--impl` now exits 2. The new **`acceptance-proven`** gate (gates **75 → 76**) renders `N/M live` wherever gates run, keeping **three distinct nothing-declared refusals** apart so “nothing declared” never reads like “declared and clean”; it ships at severity **warn** and that ceiling is **permanent by design** — `maddu ci pin` structurally refuses warn gates, because the actor who can green a proof can re-declare the goal underneath it. The gate **executes nothing**. There is **no re-baseline verb**: re-declaring destroys proofs, and the only route back to green is observing the new RED and then the new GREEN. Honest by construction — **a weak oracle proven RED→GREEN is still a weak oracle**, the guarantee is **endpoint equality, not continuous immutability**, **only the declared sets are bound**, and the full residual list ships as an export (`ACCEPTANCE_HONEST_LIMITS`) that no readout may narrow. Team-sync is **refused rather than degraded**: a partitioned spine has no single order in which a RED provably precedes a GREEN. Contract **1.18.0 → 1.19.0**; the W1 diff funnel went CLEAN at round 6 and the gate funnel at round 10, both under explicitly adjudicated boundaries, with 43 plan-round findings adjudicated before implementation; six suites (acceptance-core 34, derive 34, observe 47, record 36, wiring 67, proven-gate 45); self-test **215/215**.',
    note: 'The strongest artifact yet for the thesis this whole project rests on: a green checkmark that can say “this command was seen to exit nonzero before it exited zero, and the thing judging it did not change.” It is also the most carefully bounded — read the honest limits beside it, because what it does not close is larger than what it does.',
